## Summary

I shipped a production-polished, native Apple SwiftUI parity of `TelemetryGrid.tsx` — **8 files** in `apps/apple/TeslaSync/feature-views/`, following the exact architecture of the sibling `VehicleStatePanel/0287` (same web directory):

- **`.Format.swift`** — pure SI ports of `formatDistance`/`formatSpeed`/`formatTemperature` + `fmtInt`/`fmtNumber` (km·mi / km/h·mph / °C·°F, locale grouping, half-up rounding, per-quantity precision, no-space temp rule).
- **`.Adapter.swift`** — pure projection: the six tiles (Battery, Speed, Inside, Odometer, Charger, Sentry) with exact value/tone/sub branches + accessibility.
- **`.Model.swift`** — P1/S8 source seam, `@Observable` model, P1/S11 `view.opened`, P1/S10 facade, stale auto-refresh.
- **`.swift` / `.Views.swift`** — bare responsive grid (matching web; chip/banner only when not live), InfoTile glass cards, loading/empty/error chrome, all token-driven (P1/S9), no Tailwind ports, no raw hex.
- **`.Previews.swift`** (7 states), **`.strings`** (i18n), **`.Tests.swift`** (28 XCTest cases).

### Verification (all run, real output)
- **Isolated iOS build+test**: `BUILD SUCCEEDED` / `TEST SUCCEEDED` — **28 tests, 0 failures**.
- **Isolated macOS build+test**: `BUILD SUCCEEDED` / `TEST SUCCEEDED` — **28 tests, 0 failures**.
- `swiftlint --strict`: **0 violations** (3850 files). `swiftformat --lint apps/apple`: **0/4080**. `check-placeholders`: **0**.
- My files produce **zero** compiler diagnostics in the full iOS *and* macOS builds.

I built the `Shared.xcframework` via Gradle, ran `xcodegen`, and verified the surface in isolation (only `Sources/` + the TelemetryGrid files compiled as module `TeslaSync` against the real framework) — a throwaway spec I generated, ran, and removed.

### ⚠️ STATUS = BLOCKED (full-scheme gate)
The full `xcodebuild -scheme TeslaSync[/-macOS] build test` fails (`IOS_EXIT=65`, `MAC_EXIT=65`) — **before TelemetryGrid is reached** — due to **pre-existing, committed, out-of-scope** duplicate public type declarations in sibling surfaces sharing the single app module:
- `RecentDrivesListWidget.*` **vs** `RecentDrivesSection.*` and `StateTimelineWidget.*` **vs** `StateTimeline.*` each declare the same 4 type names → 8 `"… is ambiguous for type lookup"` errors (+ duplicate `XCTestCase` names).

These are committed at HEAD; the only untracked files in the slot are my 8 deliverables + the log. They are **explicitly out of scope** ("Other surfaces in the same feature") and **outside the prompt's allowed files** (`TelemetryGrid.*` + the log), so I cannot fix them without violating scope.

